        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "7b01ea6f-9c16-5a18-aa04-9a06346ca48e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: 1994–95 FA Cup, 2008 FA Cup victory\n- People: Joe Royle, Harry Redknapp\n- Organizations: Everton, Portsmouth, Central Coast Mariners, Wimborne Town, Southern Football League\n- Roles: manager, advisor, director\n\nFacts:\n- The 1994–95 FA Cup was the 50th FA Cup officially held since the six-year suspension caused by World War II.\n- Everton manager Joe Royle won the 1994–95 FA Cup and was the last English-born manager to lift the FA Cup until 2008.\n- Harry Redknapp managed Portsmouth to the 2008 FA Cup victory, ending the gap since Joe Royle's win with Everton.\n- Harry Redknapp is an advisor to Central Coast Mariners.\n- Harry Redknapp is a director at Southern Football League club Wimborne Town.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
